{"title":"2024 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_DDM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by DDM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Central_Valley_Math_Circle_(Goes_through_full_thought_process)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Central Valley Math Circle (Goes through full thought process)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Math-X_(First_fully_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Math-X (First fully understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(A_Clever_Explanation_You’ll_Get_Instantly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (A Clever Explanation You’ll Get Instantly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve_(crystal_clear)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve (crystal clear)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_NiuniuMaths_(Easy_to_understand!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by NiuniuMaths (Easy to understand!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_OmegaLearn.org\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn.org</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_[Very_Slow_and_Hard_to_Follow]\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CosineMethod [Very Slow and Hard to Follow]</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Dr._David\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Dr. David</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">19</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">20</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SquishBJ_(AIME_Qualifier)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">21</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SquishBJ (AIME Qualifier)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-22\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">22</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jordan owns 15 pairs of sneakers. Three fifths of the pairs are red and the rest are white. Two thirds of the pairs are high-top and the rest are low-top. The red high-top sneakers make up a fraction of the collection. What is the least possible value of this fraction?\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2024-amc-8-q19.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/54/2024-amc-8-q19.png/500px-2024-amc-8-q19.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"500\" height=\"143\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/54/2024-amc-8-q19.png/750px-2024-amc-8-q19.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/5/54/2024-amc-8-q19.png/1000px-2024-amc-8-q19.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/2/3520d12672cbafb0e0477d90f2f074d3d52430ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 0\\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\dfrac{1}{5} \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\dfrac{4}{15} \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\dfrac{1}{3} \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\dfrac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"380\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jordan has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> high top sneakers, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> white sneakers. We would want as many white high-top sneakers as possible, so we set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> high-top sneakers to be white. Then, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78d4c8d5729ac14729a48514741c49451005211a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10-6=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> red high-top sneakers, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/2303d77807bb9a85d38ca962a500bdd5927c6762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\dfrac{4}{15}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"40\" height=\"49\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first start by finding the number of red and white sneakers. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/3/743cd8dc4f0d19bd732b58a21646ffc4510bf4d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{5} \\times 15=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" /> red sneakers, so 6 are white. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/1/fc17b44e76e40af3a39eb49917f3c6e537b947ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3} \\times 15=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" /> are high top sneakers, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are low top sneakers. Now think about <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> slots, and the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are labeled high-top sneakers. If we insert the last <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sneakers as red sneakers, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> leftover red sneakers. Putting those <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> sneakers as high top sneakers, we have our answer as C, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/0/2303d77807bb9a85d38ca962a500bdd5927c6762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\dfrac{4}{15}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"40\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>-ermwhatthesigma\n</p><p><br />\n-slight change by the-guy-with-the\"W\"hairline-and-a-not-goofy-looking-gyat-with-so-much-recoil-it-bounces-to-the-nearest-blackhole...\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1901fcf8d56398b30216bff3c0abc28eb879fbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{3}{5}\\cdot 15 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"38\" /> red pairs of sneakers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> white pairs. There are also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0af450f2d3dc88fd0b9fd209376c757edbf40639.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{2}{3}\\cdot 15 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" /> high-top pairs of sneakers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> low-top pairs. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of red high-top sneakers and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of white high-top sneakers. It follows that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/0/620f3bf1f05573d2e78cfb2fa3cf9b9e9eb3828f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> red pairs of low-top sneakers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/6/e565402329d24ea447505049434f18faa744f430.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6-r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> white pairs. \nWe must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/0/5100d0e6f89e83834349dde6e04035a55f113b09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-r \\leq 5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" /> in order to have a valid amount of white sneakers. Solving this inequality gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/4/f14ac1d9a882b658a919f0fce75058723dc9c1b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\geq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />, so the smallest possible value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This means that there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/7/697feca548bd97662d29974e67463bcdbe531535.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-4=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> pairs of low-top red sneakers, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pairs of low-top white sneakers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pairs of high top white sneakers. This checks out perfectly, so the smallest fraction is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/b/8abb996dde8b24e5c97b217cf8cc6e3fd4173bc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{4}{15}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"75\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>-hola\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/e/8fedeb4e36aca05244818fe0d5ce3dbca044c642.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 \\times \\frac{3}{5}=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />, which is the number of red pairs of sneakers. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/1/fc17b44e76e40af3a39eb49917f3c6e537b947ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3} \\times 15=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" />, so there are ten pairs of high-top sneakers.  If there are ten high-top sneakers, there are five low top sneakers. To have the lowest amount of high-top red sneakers, all five of the low-top sneakers need to be red. There are four red sneakers remaining so they have to be high-top. So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/b/8abb996dde8b24e5c97b217cf8cc6e3fd4173bc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{4}{15}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"75\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>Answer by AliceDubbleYou\n</p><p>-Minor edit by angieeverfree\n</p><p>-Minor edit by SmartyDigits\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the number of red high-top sneakers be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Making a two way table we get:\n</p>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"4\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\">\n<caption>Two-way table\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>Red\n</th>\n<th>White\n</th>\n<th>Total\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th>High-top\n</th>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /></td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/552f7934039e148cff4c1aedee0f06ba6940228d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /></td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th>Low-top\n</th>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/f/00f6c152cf4fa5e6ac7a9776f981008d0ec735d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /></td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/251b9a04e21dc689a1f60a6559f35939d80137fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /></td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th>Total\n</th>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /></td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /></td>\n<td><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>From the table we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/c/22c1369143b1d9a234717f0a16c9b1d9c9c40a8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\leq x\\leq 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />. Therefore the minimum value is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/7/2e7d65cfa316d639c9267398009812f3eb45fea9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/b/8abb996dde8b24e5c97b217cf8cc6e3fd4173bc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{4}{15}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"75\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~Seafowl23\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https:/